# chord mode on Steps (a melodic track): hold a step and tap SEQ, and the keys write that step's chord - its notes
# only (its length stays) - on past the step's own release; OCT moves the keys' octave; the step written is the
# one held, in the bar and pattern it was held in (another pattern picked meanwhile is not written); SEQ again
# ends it, and so does leaving Steps (SELECT to Bar)
wait 300
turn ALGO 1
expect trk 2
notes 2 1 1 4 100 60
expect slen 2 1 16
key w0 down
wait 30
tap SEQ
wait 30
key w0 up
wait 30
key 9 down
wait 30
key 11 down
wait 30
key 9 up
key 11 up
wait 30
expect note 2 1 1 62
expect slen 2 1 16
tap OCT+
wait 30
tapkey 9
wait 30
expect note 2 1 1 74
spin K1 1
wait 30
tapkey 14
wait 30
expect note 2 1 1 79
expect note 2 2 1 0
spin K1 -1
wait 30
tap SEQ
wait 30
tapkey 11
wait 30
expect note 2 1 1 79
# leaving Steps ends it: back on Steps a key is a step again, not the chord
key w0 down
wait 30
tap SEQ
wait 30
key w0 up
wait 30
turn SELECT 1
wait 60
expect page Bar
turn SELECT -1
wait 60
expect page Steps
tapkey 11
wait 30
expect note 2 1 1 79
